What about using #pragma omp for simd private(i) instead of the pragma + __pragma() ? Edit: since OpenMP 4 doesn't seem to be an option for you, you can manually split your loop to get rid of the #pragma omp for by just computing the index limits by hand using omp_get_num_threads() and omp_get_thread_num() , and then keep the ivdep for the per-thread loop. Edit 2: since I'm a nice guy and since this is boilerplate (more common when programming in MPI, but still) but quite annoying to get right when you do it for the first time, here is a possible solution: #pragma omp parallel
{
    int n = 4096;
    int tid = omp_get_thread_num();
    int nth = omp_get_num_threads();
    int chunk = n / nth;
    int beg = tid * chunk + min( tid, n % nth );
    int end = ( tid + 1 ) * chunk + min( tid + 1, n % nth );
    #pragma ivdep
    for ( int i = beg; i < end; i++ ) {
        vC[i] = vA[i] + SCALAR * vB[i];
    }
}

