answers.body:
There are some problems with your code (e.g. local_histogram is uninitialized, number of threads in the current team was not correctly obtained,incorrect 2D array allocation, summing of local_histogram was not correct), but you do not need to do it manually, OpenMP can do it for you properly using reduction: void compute_histogram(float *numbers, int number_count, int *histogram, int number_bins) {    
    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:histogram[:number_bins])
    for (int x = 0; x < number_count; x++) {
        float read_num = numbers[x];
        histogram[(int)(read_num / (20.0 / number_bins))]++;
    }        
}

